$\mathrm{F}, \mathrm{Br}, \mathrm{I} \rightarrow \mathrm{Gr} 17$ elements; O, Se → Gr 16 elements
For isoelectronic species, more negative charge results in larger ionic radius and ionic radius of same charged species increases down the group.

\therefore \mathrm{I}^{-}>\mathrm{Se}^{2-}>\mathrm{Br}^{-}>\mathrm{O}^{2-}>\mathrm{F}^{-}
